+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a newly rendered sheet is admitted to the preview cache, the system SHALL place it in the cold queue (the queue of sheets requested exactly once).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a request hits a cached sheet held in the cold queue, the system SHALL move that sheet to the hot queue (the queue of sheets requested more than once).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a request hits a cached sheet held in the hot queue, the system SHALL refresh that sheet's recency within the hot queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When a request for a key held in the ghost list (keys of sheets evicted from the cold queue) results in a newly rendered sheet, the system SHALL admit that sheet directly to the hot queue and SHALL retain that key on the ghost list.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When the preview cache must evict sheets to remain within 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict cold-queue sheets before hot-queue sheets.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: When evicting from the cold queue, the system SHALL evict the sheet that has been held in that queue the longest; when evicting from the hot queue, the system SHALL evict the least recently used sheet.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When the hot queue exceeds its configured share of the 12 GiB cache budget, the system SHALL move the least recently used hot-queue sheet to the tail of the cold queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: When the preview worker replaces cached sheets, the system SHALL NOT expose cache paths, queue membership, hit counters, or the ghost list through the preview interface.
